<metadata><name>Pacific Crest Trail Loop</name><desc>or-central-meissner-1984:86: route read from the book's text and sketch map. One trkseg per waypoint pair, in order; segment sources are in the trk desc. Geometry from OSM (ODbL, (c) OpenStreetMap contributors) and USFS EDW (public domain) where marked; 'straight' segments are off-trail connectors, not traced.</desc></metadata>
<wpt lat="43.601292" lon="-122.036453"><ele>1565.4</ele><name>Willamette Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin (as in or-vielbig-2e:290-2); confidence: high; pdf_page: 168; quote: ski to Rosary Lakes from Willamette Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.597173" lon="-122.033710"><ele>1553.6</ele><name>PCT trailhead</name><desc>source: OSM: PCT meets Highway 58 (as in 290-2); confidence: medium; pdf_page: 168</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.604112" lon="-121.996913"><ele>1748.6</ele><name>Lower Rosary Lake, north end</name><desc>source: as in 290-2; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 168; quote: ski to Rosary Lakes from Willamette Pass</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.613303" lon="-122.005537"><ele>1884.0</ele><name>Divide (PCT at the Tye Trail junction, north of the Rosary Lakes)</name><desc>source: OSM node 980046594, PCT meets Tye Trail on the saddle above North Rosary Lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 168; book_elev_ft: 6200; quote: The marked trail continues on past Rosary Lakes, climbing uphill to the divide which is 6,200'.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.639895" lon="-122.010009"><ele>1715.2</ele><name>PCT meets Maiden Peak Trail #3861</name><desc>source: OSM node 5274506639; the sketch's PCT runs north to here before turning west; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 169</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.625812" lon="-122.046372"><ele>1507.0</ele><name>Maiden Peak Trail meets Gold Lake Road</name><desc>source: OSM node 2934688943, just south of Gold Lake; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 168; quote: From here the trail drops down for about 4 miles to Gold Lake.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.605964" lon="-122.048016"><ele>1529.8</ele><name>Gold Lake Road at Highway 58 (Gold Lake Sno-Park)</name><desc>source: OSM node 2934688911; confidence: high; pdf_page: 168; quote: Follow the Gold Lake road back to the Gold Lake Sno-park or to Willamette Pass.</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.597173" lon="-122.033710"><ele>1553.6</ele><name>PCT trailhead on Highway 58</name><desc>source: OSM node 980046400; confidence: medium; pdf_page: 169</desc></wpt>
<wpt lat="43.601292" lon="-122.036453"><ele>1565.4</ele><name>Willamette Pass Sno-Park</name><desc>source: DB trailhead pin; confidence: high; pdf_page: 168</desc></wpt>
